Upgrade procedure for Expat

Source:
  https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/releases/download/R_VERSION/expat-VERSION.tar.xz
  Replace R_VERSION with the underscore-separated release tag (e.g. R_2_10_0)
  and VERSION with the dotted version (e.g. 2.10.0).

To upgrade:

1. Download the release archive and verify its published digest/signature.
2. Import the extracted sources into vendor/expat/dist in a separate worktree.
   Remove the paths listed in MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist before staging.  Compare the
   trimmed file set with the previous import and review new/removed files.
   Keep all imported files otherwise identical to upstream.
3. Tag the import vendor/expat/dist/VERSION, then use
   git subtree merge -P contrib/expat vendor/expat/dist on each target branch.
4. Review lib/libexpat/Makefile for upstream source-list and header changes.
   Update the version strings in lib/libexpat/expat_config.h and review new
   configure macros.  Keep the native library name and ABI version.
5. Build lib/libexpat and test a consumer against the generated bsdxml.h.
   Run the upstream regression suite from the untrimmed release sources.
6. Record security fixes in a separate UPDATING commit and update the version
   table at https://github.com/MidnightBSD/src/wiki/Vendor-Branches.

Local patches:

  None in the imported sources as of Expat 2.10.0.  MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist and
  this file are downstream metadata and must not enter the vendor branch.

Native integration outside the imported subtree:

  lib/libexpat/Makefile builds libbsdxml (SHLIB_MAJOR=4), generates bsdxml.h
  by replacing Expat_INCLUDED with _BSD_XML_H_ and expat_external.h with
  bsdxml_external.h, and adjusts the COPYING reference.  Since Expat 2.9.0,
  xcs.c must be compiled separately; upstream no longer includes xcsinc.c.

  lib/libexpat/expat_config.h provides the native configuration, including
  machine/endian.h and platform entropy sources.  XML_ATTR_INFO and
  XML_MIN_SIZE were disabled here before upstream removed those features.

Notes:

  MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist omits CMake/configure support and non-native platform
  files.  Use an untrimmed archive for upstream build-system tests.
